  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 200.A42, the audit risk model (Audit Risk = Risk of Material Misstatement x Detection Risk) requires that when both inherent risk and control risk are high, detection risk must be set low to keep overall audit risk acceptably low. This means the auditor must perform more persuasive, extensive, and timely substantive procedures.
Wrong (A): Setting detection risk high when the risk of material misstatement is already high would result in unacceptably high overall audit risk.
Wrong (C): Detection risk is the auditor''s compensating lever and must move inversely to the risk of material misstatement, not mirror it.
