-- Q308: Audit Sampling [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 530.A24, the projected misstatement in MUS is calculated by determining the tainting percentage: ($400 - $320) / $400 = 20%. The projected misstatement is 20% x $80,000 sampling interval = $16,000. This projection estimates how much misstatement the sample item represents across the population stratum.
Wrong (A): $80 is simply the raw dollar difference ($400 - $320) without applying the tainting percentage to the sampling interval, which would understate the projected misstatement.
Wrong (C): $20,000 would result from incorrectly applying 25% (dividing $80 by $320 instead of $400) to the sampling interval.
Wrong (D): $80,000 equals the full sampling interval, which would only apply if the item were 100% misstated (tainting of 100%).$EXPL$
WHERE id = 308;

