  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 530.A7, a higher expected population deviation rate increases the required sample size in attributes sampling. The auditor must test more items to distinguish between the expected rate and the tolerable rate with the desired level of confidence.
Wrong (B): Increasing the tolerable deviation rate decreases sample size under AU-C 530.A6 because a wider tolerance requires fewer items to confirm the rate falls within acceptable bounds.
